WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.680
I love telling myself that size doesn’t&nbsp;
matter, but today that’s all we’re going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.040
to talk about. Because we’re going&nbsp;
from the tiniest creatures in one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:14.040
piece to behemoths that are so big, Mount&nbsp;
Everest wouldn’t even reach their knees.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:19.200
But first, here is the smallest character&nbsp;
ever in One Piece. This is Mansherry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.800
the princess of the Tontatta. The&nbsp;
Tontatta tribe are tiny dwarves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:29.220
the size of a chopstick that are actually so&nbsp;
small and fast, that the citizens of Dressrosa&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:34.440
rarely even see them. And Mansherry is&nbsp;
the smallest even among these dwarfs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:41.880
at only 20 centimeter or about 8 inches tall:&nbsp;
which is barely even the height of a dinner fork!

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:46.740
But moving from the smallest character to the&nbsp;
smallest Straw Hat, we have Tony Tony Chopper.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:52.020
Now obviously Chopper can vary in size,&nbsp;
because his zoan type devil fruit allows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:59.580
Chopper to change forms. And in his monster&nbsp;
form he is x tall, but for our purposes we’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:06.780
talking about Chopper in his base form: This&nbsp;
adorable baseball bat-sized doctor measures 90&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:11.520
centimeters or just under 3 feet. He’s just&nbsp;
a little guy and we love him most that way!

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.780
Compared to that, Monkey D. Luffy,&nbsp;
our main protagonist, is a true giant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:22.200
who comes in at 1.74 meters…when he’s not&nbsp;
stretched out that is. That’s about 5 foot 7,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:29.280
so about the height of the average man worldwide,&nbsp;
which seems too specific to be a coincidence. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:33.960
thinking of Luffy staring down like…literally&nbsp;
any of the antagonists of the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:39.780
we can tell things are about to get crazy&nbsp;
when it comes to how tall some characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:45.120
truly are. We’re not even talking about things&nbsp;
like the sea kings or the gates of justice yet.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:52.380
First though, still possible in our real world&nbsp;
is Shanks. This Yonkou stands 2 meters tall or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:59.520
about 6 foot 5. And while this IS pretty tall,&nbsp;
there ARE people who are this tall. For a frame&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:04.860
of reference, 2 meters is about the height of an&nbsp;
average door. Which means that from here on out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:10.740
every character we discuss is going to have to&nbsp;
lean down reaaally far whenever they walk into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:16.860
a room. Or in some cases they just have no&nbsp;
hope of ever fitting through a door at all.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:22.560
Which makes me wonder: Are buildings in the&nbsp;
One Piece world just…bigger than in real life?

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:30.420
Like, what about people like Jinbe, who’s a&nbsp;
whopping 3 meters tall. For the mathematically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:36.900
impaired that’s one and a half Shankses -&nbsp;
or 10 feet tall! And this makes sense given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:41.700
that in general, a lot of fishmen tend to be&nbsp;
bigger and stronger than the average human.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:46.980
But on top of that Jinbe is also whale&nbsp;
shark fishman. In case you don’t know:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:52.200
whale sharks just so happen to be the&nbsp;
biggest species of fish in the world…well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:58.260
our world anyway. so it’s no surprise that&nbsp;
he towers above many of his crew mates. - But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:03.720
it’s of course NOTHING compared to some of the&nbsp;
absolutely massive sea creatures still coming up.

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:09.600
But for now we’re sticking to people as we go to&nbsp;
another one of the Yonkou - Luffy’s biggest rival,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:20.040
Blackbeard. Marshall D. Teach is 3 meters and&nbsp;
44cm tall, which is over 11 feet! Hmmm…I never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:25.980
imagined that Blackbeard was that much taller than&nbsp;
Jinbe. I mean, before now I always wondered how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:32.760
he was ever able to give Shanks his signature&nbsp;
scars - and height isn’t everything, but he’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:39.360
almost TWICE as TALL as Shanks. But as you know,&nbsp;
he’s far from the biggest member of his crew…

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:45.000
He’s also nowhere near the size of the Shichibukai&nbsp;
Bartholomew Kuma. Whenever we see Kuma,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:50.880
he straight out towers over regular people like&nbsp;
Luffy and co, from his first meeting with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:57.180
Straw Hats on Thriller Bark to him destroying the&nbsp;
entire crew on Sabaody Archipelago. This fearsome&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:04.320
former warlord is 6.89 meters tall - two times&nbsp;
the height of the already massive Blackbeard.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:10.140
That’s 22 feet. This man is huge! We’ve heard&nbsp;
hints in the series in the most recent arc that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:15.420
Kuma comes from a special race of people,&nbsp;
but it’s still hard to grasp how a person&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:22.320
who’s NOT a giant, can be as tall as two&nbsp;
elephants stacked on top of each other!

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:28.920
Kaidou in his base form, though, is even&nbsp;
taller at 7.10 meters. For some reference,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:33.600
that’s about the height of a traffic&nbsp;
light. It’s no wonder that for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:37.800
fight with Luffy at Onigashima, he had&nbsp;
to take things to the rooftop. Sure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:45.840
he used the excuse of not being able to fit in&nbsp;
his crazy huge dragon form, but at 23 feet tall,,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:52.680
it’s amazing he has any clearance in his hallways&nbsp;
whatsoever. Thankfully Onigashima is big enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:58.440
to fit the Numbers, so it’s probably the only&nbsp;
building in Wano that has enough space for him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:05.460
to stretch his legs. It really makes you&nbsp;
wonder just how big Onigashima is, huh…

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:13.140
Big Mom stays true to her name, though, being&nbsp;
8.8 meters tall. That’s almost 29 feet! She’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:18.840
about the height of a 3 story building,&nbsp;
so it’s no wonder both her children and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:24.540
her husbands are terrified of her! She really&nbsp;
takes the whole cake, being the biggest of all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:29.460
the yonkou. It’s no wonder she’s sour about&nbsp;
Lola’s engagement to Loki, the Prince of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:34.920
Giants falling through. After all, if she had&nbsp;
a few more giants around, she might finally be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:39.420
able to realize her dream of having everyone&nbsp;
sitting around a table at her own level.

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:46.020
Shirahoshi, the Mermaid Princess of&nbsp;
Fishman Island…is just absurdly big.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:54.840
She’s 11.87 meters or 39 feet tall. It’s&nbsp;
wild that she’s so cowardly given that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.840 --> 00:06:00.300
could look a Brachiosaurus in the eye, no&nbsp;
problem. It’s amazing that Vander Decken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:06.300
was able to torment her so much, considering&nbsp;
that she could probably pick him up and yeet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:11.220
him all the way to the surface if she&nbsp;
really wanted. Looking at her parents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:19.560
King Neptune and Queen Orohime…I mean, I don’t&nbsp;
even understand how she’s this big! Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:26.400
she’s nothing compared to the fearsome sea&nbsp;
kings she commands…but more on those later.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:32.580
From here on out, every single entry is official&nbsp;
giant sized. Hajrudin, a member of the giant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:39.780
pirates and now one of Luffy’s subordinates in&nbsp;
the Grand Fleet is 22 meters tall. That’s 72&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:45.300
feet or about the height of two telephone poles&nbsp;
stacked on top of each other. It really just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:50.820
makes it much more impressive how easily Luffy&nbsp;
was able to take Hajrudin out at the Dressrosa&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:57.840
Coliseum. And even more impressive that Luffy has&nbsp;
a vertical leap that’s 13 times his own height.

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:05.220
The Thousand Sunny, the Straw Hat’s ship is&nbsp;
56 meters or 183 feet at its tallest point.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:10.680
It makes sense that boats in the One Piece world&nbsp;
have to be huge given how massive the characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:16.020
we’ve already talked about are. Even being as&nbsp;
big as it is compared to their original ship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:21.960
the Going Merry, the Sunny is absolutely&nbsp;
dwarfed by other ships like Big Mom’s flagship.

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:29.100
Oars, the ancient giant, was 67 meters or&nbsp;
219 feet. This character was resurrected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:33.780
as a zombie by Gekko Moriah’s shadow&nbsp;
ability. It’s no wonder Moriah wanted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:38.700
this deceased warrior to be the center&nbsp;
piece of his undead army. Laying down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:45.300
Oars would measure the same length as a 747’s&nbsp;
wingspan. And if that’s hard to imagine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:51.060
let’s just say that jumbo jets…are&nbsp;
called “jumbo” jets for a good reason.

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:59.820
But even this ancient warrior can’t measure up&nbsp;
to Wadatsumi, the giant tiger blowfish fishman.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:08.940
He’s 80 meters or 262 feet, which made him a&nbsp;
terrifying ally of the New Fishman pirates. It’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:15.540
wild that he’s based on a blowfish, too, because&nbsp;
that means he can puff himself up to become even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:22.200
bigger. He’s by far the biggest fishman, but&nbsp;
he’s nothing compared to the biggest giant:

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:27.960
Sanjuan Wolf. One of Blackbeard’s Ten&nbsp;
Titanic Captains, Sanjuan Wolf is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:32.220
only giant who’s confirmed to have eaten&nbsp;
a devil fruit. And whatever devil fruit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:42.180
it is…made him absolutely massive. Wolf is&nbsp;
183 meters tall. That’s 600 feet. And since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:46.440
these numbers are just getting straight up&nbsp;
hard to imagine now, that’s the height of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:52.140
the Space Needle. Sanjuan Wolf is so huge&nbsp;
that even though he’s a devil fruit user,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:58.200
he can freely enter the ocean. He won’t drown&nbsp;
because he’s tall enough that his feet reach the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:03.240
bottom and he can just stand in the sea without&nbsp;
having to worry about not being able to swim.

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:16.020
But now we go from the sea all the way up to the&nbsp;
sky, with one of One Piece’s longest creatures:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:20.880
Nola, the snake who’s lived in Shandora&nbsp;
for 400 years! In all of that time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:25.680
Nola grew up from the cute little reptile&nbsp;
we see in Nolan and Calgara’s flashback&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:34.260
to this! Easily able to swallow Luffy whole.&nbsp;
This serpent is 200 meters or 656 feet long,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:39.180
making him one of the oldest AND&nbsp;
biggest animals in all of One Piece.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:46.680
However, Nola isn’t as big as Surume, a&nbsp;
300 meter tall Kraken who Luffy befriends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:52.560
on the way to Fishman Island. That&nbsp;
translates to 984 feet or just shy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:57.300
of the Eiffel Tower! As the crew descended&nbsp;
beneath the Red Line toward Fishman Island,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.300 --> 00:10:03.060
they didn’t expect to encounter a sea&nbsp;
creature so ridiculously big. Thankfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:09.060
though, Luffy makes friends everywhere he goes,&nbsp;
and soon the crew had a new many-armed ally.

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:15.360
But from the entrance to the New World, now we&nbsp;
go back to the entrance of the Grand Line with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:19.740
Laboon! The giant whale that swallowed the&nbsp;
crew as soon as they entered the Grand Line&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:27.780
through Reverse Mountain measures 400 meters&nbsp;
or 1312 feet from tail to head. Given how much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:33.060
different he looks from when he was a baby, who&nbsp;
knows if Brook will even recognize this behemoth?

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:39.420
Apparently at the beginning of the Grand Line,&nbsp;
Oda was just really on a kick of introducing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:45.840
absolutely huge monsters. Because now we go from&nbsp;
Laboon to the Island Eater Fish, the massive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:57.780
island sized that almost swallowed Little Garden.&nbsp;
This 715 meter or 2345 feet beast is almost as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.780 --> 00:11:03.720
long as the Burj Khalifa is tall: you know, the&nbsp;
tallest building in the entire world. Luckily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:10.440
Dorry and Brogy had some giant sized strength&nbsp;
to be able to defeat it and save the day.

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:17.460
But now we move from giant creatures to the&nbsp;
biggest ship in the series: the Noah. Now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:25.020
we’re at a scale so big that meters and feet&nbsp;
just aren’t going to cut it. At 2500 meters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:34.440
it’ll be easier to just say 2.5 kilometers. And&nbsp;
we also ahve our first entry over a mile at 8202&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:41.880
feet. A mile as we all know is 5280 feet…wait is&nbsp;
that how the Imperial measurement system works?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:48.300
Why would it be 5280? Anyway - the Noah&nbsp;
is a massive ark built with the intention&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:56.460
of someday bringing the citizens of Fishman&nbsp;
Island up to the surface…unfortunately Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.460 --> 00:12:01.500
destroyed it. Hopefully it gets rebuilt&nbsp;
before he also destroys Fishman Island!

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:11.160
But even the Noah doesn’t stack up to the biggest&nbsp;
door in all of anime. The Gates of Justice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:16.440
which we don’t have official measurements for,&nbsp;
but doing some real-life mathematics we can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:24.360
estimate to be about 3 Kilometers or nearly 2&nbsp;
miles high, including the underwater portions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:29.700
The World Government has done some impressive&nbsp;
things to be able to control the entire world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:36.420
but among the most impressive? This&nbsp;
truly remarkable feat of engineering.

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:40.740
But now we go from a man-made structure&nbsp;
to one that is seemingly all natural:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:49.800
The giant skull that Kaidou lives in on&nbsp;
Onigashima. This thing is 3.7 kilometers high&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:57.780
and over 2 miles high. It’s so massive it really&nbsp;
makes you wonder how big this ancient giant was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.780 --> 00:13:05.460
when it was alive. Which is why we calculated it!&nbsp;
You see…if you take the hypotenuse and multiply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.460 --> 00:13:09.900
by the square root of the quotient and the factor&nbsp;
in the permutations of the prime meridian…Okay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:16.260
actually it was a lot simpler than that.&nbsp;
If we assume an ancient giant has similar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.260 --> 00:13:21.360
proportions to a human, its total height&nbsp;
should be about 8 times the size of its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:29.820
head. So we can assume that his full height&nbsp;
when alive was 29,320 meters or approximately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:37.020
18 miles tall. Absurdly huge…but still not&nbsp;
the biggest thing we’ll get to on this list.

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:41.520
But first, some huge things that are&nbsp;
just a *bit* smaller than that. You see,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:47.040
it just feels wrong to describe the Sea Kings&nbsp;
as small in any way, even when speaking in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:54.300
relative terms. But at an average length&nbsp;
of 5 kilometers or about 3 miles…it’s no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.300 --> 00:14:00.240
wonder that Poseidon’s power to control these&nbsp;
leviathans is considered an ancient weapon.

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:13.320
Twice as big as that, though, is the Red&nbsp;
Line. at 10 kilometers or about 6 miles high,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:13.980 --> 00:14:19.500
the Red Line is taller than Mt. Everest. Which&nbsp;
is even more impressive when you consider that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:26.820
the Red Line is like a Mt. Everest that stretches&nbsp;
around the entire circumference of the planet. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.820 --> 00:14:33.840
can really see how having that in real life would&nbsp;
put a damper on any international travel plans. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:33.840 --> 00:14:41.340
also makes it even more impressive that Fisher&nbsp;
Tiger scaled this thing with his bare hands.

00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:47.940
But now we’re getting to the official&nbsp;
biggest things in the series: Zunesha,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:52.920
including his legs that can easily reach the&nbsp;
sea floor so that he can walk around the ocean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.920 --> 00:15:02.820
is 35 kilometers tall. That’s about 21.7&nbsp;
miles or in other words…the size of four&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.705 --> 00:15:12.060
Mt. Everests. That really makes me feel&nbsp;
worse for Ryunosuke…rest in peace, friend…

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:16.020
This one is more of an estimation -&nbsp;
these shadows of the Shandian Warriors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:17.460 --> 00:15:21.000
though just the shadows of&nbsp;
normal sized people measure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:28.860
about 44 kilometers or 27 miles high. And&nbsp;
a lot of people confuse them with these:

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:37.620
The Florian Triangle Monsters. These mysterious&nbsp;
and unexplained creatures are based on Japanese&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:50.400
yokai called Umibozu, enormous sea monsters&nbsp;
said to drown sailors. AT our best estimate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:50.400 --> 00:15:57.480
we can guess that these entities&nbsp;
are 54 kilometers or 33 miles high,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.480 --> 00:16:05.100
making them the BIGGEST thing in all of One&nbsp;
Piece. And in addition to this mystery there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:09.900
are tons of other unexplained things in One&nbsp;
Piece, and you can check them all out in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:15.660
video where we go over every mystery that still&nbsp;
needs answered before the end of the series.

